{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/921538-simplifying-beasts-for-use-in-other-games-as-npcs","id":921538,"title":"Simplifying Beasts for use in other games as NPCs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-26T10:07:53-07:00","id":921538,"title":"Simplifying Beasts for use in other games as NPCs","content":"I'm running a Mage game and I'd like to make use of a Beast NPC, but I don't have the actual Beast book and don't really want to stat up the full template. What I'd love is a resource like the Demon Storyteller's Guide, which provided little simplified mechanical writeups of various other gamelines for use as NPCs in a Demon game: for example, &quot;Prometheans have powers dealing with transformation and change, here's some specific flavorful things they can do. They cause Disquiet, which you can represent with this custom Condition. They have a fuel resource called Pyros which they can spend 1 for 1 to buff their stats.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mortal Remains for Hunter has crossover-friendly content like that too, and apparently Beast is belatedly getting a section for that but it's not out yet, so.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to represent a Begotten character in another game, what are the most important details of the template? What are some of their signature powers and abilities, like a vampire's Dominate or a Promethean's electricity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:20:25-07:00","id":921613,"title":"","content":"Ok.... so the important stuff:<br /> <br /> 1) Beasts feed by causing shock in humans (each has a preferred method but one of their basic splat types is the general nature of this such as collecting for their hoard, or punishing transgressions). The better fed they are, the most extravagant/complex feedings need to be to work. How well fed a Beast is impacts their powers.<br /> <br /> 2) Their power stat is called Lair, and is actually a Lair for their Hunger (the monster of legend they embody), but it exists in the realm of dreams. As they grow in power, their Lair grows in size and danger. Beasts can bring their Lair into the real world to impede their enemies; which is easier in places that resonant with their legend. So a kraken themed Beast is more dangerous in watery coves and shipwrecks because they can warp the environment in their favor. Beasts that group together can share Lairs.<br /> <br /> 3) Beasts have an affinity for (most) supernatural creatures. This affinity allows them to overcome suspicion of outsiders and join other supernatural communities. This has benefits for the Beast (they can feed more easily by &quot;snacking&quot; on how other supernaturals obtain their energies, and lets them learn new powers), and benefits for the supernaturals that ally with them (both some mechanical boosts, and just having an ally with powers).<br /> <br /> 4) Beasts have powers called Atavisms. These are stronger the hungrier the Beast is. These are blunt, dangerous, and innate things. A dragon can breath fire. A giant has the strength to toss boulders. Etc. To normal eyes, the Begotten is still human, but is performing acts that evoke monsters of legend.<br /> <br /> 5) Beats have another set of powers called Nightmares. Nightmares allow them to influence minds, but like Atavisms are generally blunt powers; without the control of Dominate or the manipulations of Mind magic. They draw out fears and horror in humans. These are stronger when the Beast is well feed, because it allows them to be more in touch with their human side to evoke such things. Beasts can also learn Kinship Nightmares, born from seeing the fears other supernaturals cause in humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T12:31:36-07:00","id":921623,"title":"","content":"Another ability is the Skeleton Key, where a Beast can open an otherworld gate such as an Avernian Gate or Hedge Entrance, though the Beast itself has no innate sense for these gates, they need to find out their locale in other ways. The most interesting thing about the Skeleton Key ability is the Beast can also make this gateway open up to their Lair instead of what normally it would open to.<br /> <br /> A Beast that's well fed can also shift their appearance ever so slightly to make themselves look more like whatever supernatural they're bonding with, thanks to the Kinship.<br /> <br /> The main thing to remember about Beasts though is they do not class Demons (the Descent GM versions) as kin. These two actually don't mix very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}